
###  TTD:
###
### Semantic Precision:
### More owl statements would help prevent conceptual overlap
### Explicit inverse properties would make relationships clearer
### 
### Naming Conventions:
### Property naming still varies between snake_case and camelCase
### More consistency needed in abbreviations
### 
### Domain-Specific Extensions:
### The semiconductor manufacturing process hierarchy could be better integrated with design processes
### More explicit connections between design artifacts and manufacturing steps
### 
### Practical Usage Concerns:
### Need for modular structure that allows partial imports
### Balancing between complete specificity and usable simplicity
### 
### Formal Semantics:
### More explicit cardinality constraints would improve modeling precision
### Additional axioms defining rules would enhance reasoning capabilities
### 
### Validation Approach:
### Use cases should be developed to test the completeness of the ontology
### Competency questions would help verify if the ontology can answer key design questions
### 


@prefix eda: <http://example.org/eda#> .
@prefix rdf: <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#> .
@prefix rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
@prefix owl: <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#> .
@prefix xsd: <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .
@prefix qudt: <http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/> .
@prefix unit: <http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/> .
@prefix dc: <http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/> .
@prefix dct: <http://purl.org/dc/terms/> .
@prefix vann: <http://purl.org/vocab/vann/> .
@prefix foaf: <http://xmlns.com/foaf/0.1/> .
@prefix time: <http://www.w3.org/2006/time#> .
@prefix om: <http://www.ontology-of-units-of-measure.org/resource/om-2/> .
@prefix schema: <https://schema.org/> .
@prefix crsnt: <http://mlcommons.org/croissant/> .
@prefix ml: <http://example.org/ml#> .

### Ontology Declaration
<http://example.org/eda> a owl:Ontology ;
    dc:title "Integrated Electronic Design Automation Ontology" ;
    dc:description "A comprehensive ontology representing Electronic Design Automation concepts, processes, artifacts, and their relationships, merging the taxonomy_v0p5.json and eda-ontology.ttl schemas." ;
    owl:versionInfo "2.0.0" ;
    dct:created "2025-04-17"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:creator [
        a foaf:Person ;
        foaf:name "Integrated EDA Ontology Working Group" ;
    ] ;
    dct:publisher "Integrated EDA Consortium" ;
    vann:preferredNamespacePrefix "eda" ;
    vann:preferredNamespaceUri "http://example.org/eda#" .

###### Top-Level Classes ######

eda:EDAProcess a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "EDA Process" ;
    rdfs:comment "A process in the Electronic Design Automation workflow" .

eda:DesignArtifact a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Design Artifact" ;
    rdfs:comment "An artifact produced or consumed in the EDA process" .

eda:Tool a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Tool" ;
    rdfs:comment "A software tool used in the EDA process" .

eda:Metric a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Metric" ;
    rdfs:comment "A measurable attribute or figure of merit related to the design or process." .

###### Process Subclasses ######

eda:Verification a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf eda:EDAProcess ;
    rdfs:label "Verification" ;
    rdfs:comment "The process of ensuring design correctness" .

eda:LogicalSynthesis a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf eda:EDAProcess ;
    rdfs:label "Logical Synthesis" ;
    rdfs:comment "The process of converting RTL into a gate-level netlist" .

eda:LogicalDesign a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf eda:EDAProcess ;
    rdfs:label "Logical Design" ;
    rdfs:comment "The process of mapping a netlist to a logical layout" .

eda:PhysicalDesign a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf eda:EDAProcess ;
    rdfs:label "Physical Design" ;
    rdfs:comment "The process of mapping a netlist to a physical layout" .

eda:OPC a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf eda:EDAProcess ;
    rdfs:label "Optical Proximity Correction" ;
    rdfs:comment "The process of modifying mask patterns to account for lithographic distortions" .

eda:ConcurrentPhysicalOptimization a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf eda:PhysicalDesign ;
    rdfs:label "Concurrent Physical Optimization" ;
    rdfs:comment "A process that simultaneously optimizes layout, global routing, and static timing analysis using a unified objective function" .

###### Flow-Related Classes ######

eda:Flow a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf eda:DesignArtifact ;
    rdfs:label "Flow" ;
    rdfs:comment "Represents an EDA process flow execution instance with stages." .

eda:Stage a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Stage" ;
    rdfs:comment "A distinct phase or step within an EDA flow execution." .

